<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged Friday as demand remained slack, grain dealers in Kansas and Oklahoma said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no demand for wheat right now... anywhere,&quot; an Oklahoma merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Dealers said they expected demand for U.S. wheat to remain slack unless prices fall further to take into account the improved world wheat production outlook.</p>
<p>On Friday, the International Grains Council raised its forecast for 1996 world wheat production to 563 million tonnes from its previous estimate of 560 million.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against KCBT wheat, cash dollars/bu.</p>
